envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-intent
type: schema
id: intent
context: >-
  guardian/schemas — sovereign local copy. Origin: lib/node-schemas/schema.intent (shared canonical
  version, may have moved on independently since this copy was made — sovereignty means guardian
  does not depend on it at runtime, not that the two can never drift).
intent: null
summary: null
system: guardian
tags: []
exported_at: 1789235656508
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    Promoted from OPEN this pass — real grounding found while mapping copilot:
    hooks/copilot.hooks.js's own copilot-prompt hook declares seam.intentId:
    "ask|build|diagnose|navigate|note|tool|action", a fixed, real 7-value enum, and
    copilot/intents.js implements real dispatch for each (classifyIntent(), route(),
    handleNavigate/handleNote/handleTool/handleAction). Cross-checked against two other independent
    real sites using the same concept: guardian/registry-components.js's job.dispatch capability
    (hooks.in[].intent:['build','ask','forge','compile']) and guardian/lib/jobs.js's
    intentHatRouter.suggestHat(). §HONEST SHAPE NOTE — every real site above implements intent as a
    classification key (a string from a fixed vocabulary) plus dispatch functions, not as a
    per-intent data record anyone writes to a file. A .intent node therefore describes one entry in
    a real vocabulary (what it is, what it dispatches to) rather than being the executable
    classifier itself — same relationship schema.tool has to a tool's own `execute`.
  fields:
    name:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: >-
        real intent id from a system's own fixed vocabulary, e.g. 'ask', 'build', 'navigate'
        (copilot) or 'code' (guardian)
    description:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, human-readable description of what this intent covers
    system:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: >-
        real owning system whose vocabulary this intent belongs to, e.g. 'copilot', 'guardian' —
        intent vocabularies are real but per-system, not unified
    dispatchesTo:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: >-
        real handler/route this intent's classification leads to, e.g. copilot's handleNavigate,
        guardian's hat suggestion path
    command:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: >-
        real associated .command, when this intent maps to one guardian-style (e.g. job.dispatch's
        own command field)
    defaultModel:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: optional default model for this intent, when the owning system's dispatch sets one
    timeoutMs:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: optional per-intent deadline, when the owning system declares one
